---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const CAL_USERNAME = "ianhelfrich";
const CAL_EVENT = "consult-30min";
---
<Base title="Book a session" description="Schedule a tutoring consult or research call.">
  <h1>Book a session</h1>

  <p>Pick a time below. The default event is a 30-minute introductory consult. After our first call we'll set a regular cadence and discuss rates.</p>

  <p style="font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    Timezone is auto-detected. If you're outside US hours, look at the late evening slots (Atlanta time) for early-morning options in Europe/Africa, or early-morning Atlanta slots for late-evening Asia/Australia.
  </p>

  <div id="cal-embed" style="min-height: 720px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--paper-2); padding: 1rem;">
    <p style="text-align: center; padding: 2rem 1rem; color: var(--muted);">
      <strong>Booking widget initializing.</strong><br/>
      If the calendar doesn't load below in a few seconds, my Cal.com account isn't connected yet. <a href="mailto:ianthelfrich@gmail.com?subject=Booking%20request">Email me directly</a> and we'll pick a time.
    </p>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ CAL_USERNAME, CAL_EVENT }}>
    (function() {
      // Cal.com embed script; will silently no-op if the account isn't set up
      const script = document.createElement('script');
      script.src = 'https://app.cal.com/embed/embed.js';
      script.async = true;
      script.onload = function() {
        if (window.Cal) {
          window.Cal('init', { origin: 'https://cal.com' });
          window.Cal('inline', {
            elementOrSelector: '#cal-embed',
            calLink: `${CAL_USERNAME}/${CAL_EVENT}`,
            config: { theme: 'light' }
          });
          window.Cal('ui', {
            theme: 'light',
            styles: { branding: { brandColor: '#b85c38' } },
            hideEventTypeDetails: false
          });
        }
      };
      script.onerror = function() {
        document.getElementById('cal-embed').innerHTML = '<p style="text-align: center; padding: 2rem 1rem; color: var(--muted);"><strong>Cal.com is not reachable.</strong><br/>Please <a href="mailto:ianthelfrich@gmail.com?subject=Booking%20request">email me</a> directly.</p>';
      };
      document.head.appendChild(script);
    })();
  </script>

  <h2>What to expect</h2>

  <p>For the first call we'll spend 30 minutes on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>What you're working on (5-10 min, you talk)</li>
    <li>Whether I'm the right fit (5 min, I push back honestly if I'm not)</li>
    <li>What a cadence and structure could look like (10 min)</li>
    <li>Rates, scheduling logistics, and next steps (5 min)</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If we both decide to work together, follow-on sessions are billed by the hour at a rate we agree on the first call. Rates vary by client situation (graduate students get a different rate than industry clients). I'm transparent about this and we'll figure it out together.</p>

  <h2>What we won't do</h2>

  <p>I don't write your problem sets for you. I don't do your dissertation econometrics on your behalf. I will sit with you while you do the work, push back when something is wrong, and make sure you understand <em>why</em> a particular estimator is the right one for your data. That's the bargain.</p>

  <h2>Cancellations</h2>

  <p>Cancel at least 6 hours in advance via the calendar invite. Late cancellations and no-shows are charged at half the session rate (after the first call, which is free regardless).</p>
</Base>
